  "notes": "Modified cash basis for governmental activities; business-type (Water, Sewer) on accrual basis. Governmental lines from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements, and Changes in Fund Balances (Total Governmental Funds, p5); business-type lines from Statement of Revenues, Expenses, and Changes in Fund Net Position - Proprietary Funds Totals column (p7). Transfers: General Fund in 88,980 from Debt Service Fund (88,980 out), net zero in the total column; consistent both sides. Business-type roll: beginning as previously reported 4,101,412 - restatement 10,446 - loss on disposal 3,040 (nonoperating, treated as adjustment) + receipts 1,065,886 - expenses 850,843 = 4,302,969. Governmental identity: 1,757,433 + 2,121,289 - 3,535,297 = 343,425. Balance sheet (attempt 2, user rule 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the Balance Sheet - Modified Cash Basis - Governmental Funds Total column (p4), whose total 343,425 equals the government-wide governmental activities column (p1); business-type lines from the p1 Statement of Net Position business-type column; printed totals from the p1 primary government Totals column (airport authority component unit excluded); the noncurrent split (2,201,906 / 11,025) is printed on p6. Detail: General Fund budgetary schedule (p9); Debt Service Fund lines from the p5 statement column (kept: it carries the transfer-out side; it has no schedule of its own). Attempt 3 (verifier fix 2026-10-28): Water and Sewer detail now from their Budgetary Comparison Schedules - Budgetary Basis (p10-11, actual and budget; operating lines tie to Total Operating Revenues/Expenses; nonoperating interest, capital outlay and principal retirement are outside_printed_total), replacing the p7 accrual statement columns; business-type receipts Charges for Services now category Utility Charges. Proprietary cash flow statement is on p8. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
